2079600],[6.8,7.05,6.68,6.85,880300],[7.0,7.2,6.76,7.06,2717800],[7.1,7.25,6.6,6.67,2710700],[6.74,6.98,6.57,6.85,2886400]],"about":{"what":"Crown Holdings, Inc. (CCK). This chart runs from Feb 21, 2002 to Jun 28, 2002.","setup":"The stock rose about 322% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $12.65 and pulling back 24% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On May 10, 2002 it closed at $9.55, below the base's floor of $9.81, without ever closing above the base high of $12.65. Volume that day was 2.0M shares, 1.01x the prior 10-day average. It kept sliding, down to $6.30, and the chart ends at $6.85.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakdown. The stock built what looked like a base, then broke out of the bottom instead of the top. There was never a breakout to buy. When a base gives way below, the move is to stay out, or get out fast if you bought early."}}